DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ooffww__ccoonnssoollee driver provides a simple text console, using the Open
     Firmware services for input and output.  It will use the Open Firmware
     console devices set via the _i_n_p_u_t_-_d_e_v_i_c_e and _o_u_t_p_u_t_-_d_e_v_i_c_e variables.

     This driver is deprecated and only provided as a fallback console mecha‐
     nism if the real console hardware can not be driven by FreeBSD.

     In case the ooffww__ccoonnssoollee console appears to work too slowly, its respon‐
     siveness probably can be improved by including ooppttiioonnss OOFFWWCCOONNSS__PPOOLLLL__HHZZ==NN.
     When omitted, OFWCONS_POLL_HZ defaults to 4.  For example, on Sun Ultra 2
     a value of 20 or higher works best.  Too high values, on the other hand,
     can cause ooffww__ccoonnssoollee to unnecessarily consume CPU.

