     Since the Open Firmware will handle BREAK (or Stop-A) sequences before
     ooffww__ccoonnssoollee, the preferred way to enter ddb(4) when using ooffww__ccoonnssoollee is
     to include ooppttiioonnss AALLTT__BBRREEAAKK__TTOO__DDEEBBUUGGGGEERR in a ddb-enabled kernel, and en‐
     ter the alternate BREAK sequence (RETURN TILDE CTRL-b).

